        "text": "33"
      },
      {
        "y": 24.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 328.5,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Our endangered world"
      },
      {
        "y": 71.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 518.1,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "You probably already know a lot of words for talking about the environment, pollution, and so on. In"
      },
      {
        "y": 83.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 520.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "this unit we focus particularly on collocations (words that are often used together). Try to learn these"
      },
      {
        "y": 95.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 222,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "and use them in your writing."
      },
      {
        "y": 116.6,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 372.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "A Threats and potential threats to the environment"
      },
      {
        "y": 143.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 468.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Shrinking habitats1 are a threat to biodiversity2, in terms of both plants and animals, and"
      },
      {
        "y": 154.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 493.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "endangered species3 need legal protection if they are to survive. Although some climate change"
      },
      {
        "y": 165.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 496.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "sceptics4 disagree, most scientists believe that global warming5 will increase. This will encourage"
      },
      {
        "y": 176.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 502.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "polar ice to melt, resulting in rising sea levels and climatic changes. Carbon (dioxide) emissions6"
      },
      {
        "y": 187.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 503.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "from the burning of fossil fuels7 are contributing to the greenhouse effect8. In addition, population"
      },
      {
        "y": 198.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 497.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "growth exerts severe pressure on9 finite resources10, and the ecological balance11 may be upset"
      },
      {
        "y": 209.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 491.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "by uncontrolled deforestation12. Demographic projections13 suggest the world population will"
      },
      {
        "y": 220.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 512.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "continue to grow exponentially14, putting extra pressure on depleting resources15. Waste disposal16"
      },
      {
        "y": 231.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 507.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "is an increasing problem and toxic waste17 is contaminating18 many rivers and seas. Safe water may"
      },
      {
        "y": 242.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 491.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "become an increasingly precious commodity19, leading to issues of water security20. One of the"
      },
      {
        "y": 253.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 510.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "worst-case scenarios21 is that there will be no tropical rainforests left by the year 2050. Our only hope"
      },
      {
        "y": 264.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 509.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "is that pristine environments22 such as Antarctica can be protected from development and damage,"
      },
      {
        "y": 277,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 284.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "so that at least these habitats are preserved."
      },
      {
        "y": 303.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 507,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 places where animals live and breed which are decreasing in size 2 variety of different types of biological"
      },
      {
        "y": 315.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 507.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "species 3 types of animals/plants which are in danger of no longer existing 4 people who do not believe"
      },
      {
        "y": 327.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 505.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "that climate change is a serious issue 5 steady rise in average world temperatures 6 carbon dioxide gas"
      },
      {
        "y": 339.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 491.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "from factories, cars, etc. 7 coal, oil, etc. 8 warming of the Earth’s surface caused by pollution, where"
      },
      {
        "y": 351.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 509.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "gases trap and redirect heat back down to the Earth’s surface 9 puts great pressure on; formal 10 limited"
      },
      {
        "y": 363.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 512.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "resources that will eventually run out / be exhausted 11 balance of natural relationships in the environment"
      },
      {
        "y": 375.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 515.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "12 unrestricted destruction/clearing of forests 13 forecasts about the population 14 grow extremely rapidly"
      },
      {
        "y": 387.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 486.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "15 resources that are reducing 16 getting rid of waste 17 poisonous waste materials 18 poisoning"
      },
      {
        "y": 399.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 497.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(something) 19 very valuable substance 20 ability to ensure that a population has safe drinking water"
      },
      {
        "y": 411.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 419.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "21 the worst possibilities for the future 22 perfectly clean/untouched/unspoilt areas"
      },
      {
        "y": 432.4,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 372.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Responses to environmental issues and problems"
      },
      {
        "y": 450.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 367.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Look at these newspaper headlines and note the useful phrases."
      },
      {
        "y": 474.3,
        "x0": 103.3,
        "x1": 250,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "GOVERNING PARTY IN BID TO IMPROVE"
      },
      {
        "y": 485.1,
        "x0": 132.3,
        "x1": 221,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "GREEN CREDENTIALS1"
      },
      {
        "y": 487.7,
        "x0": 291.7,
        "x1": 522.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "PROPHETS OF DOOM AND GLOOM2 SHOULD LISTEN TO SCIENTIFIC"
      },
      {
        "y": 499.5,
        "x0": 349.3,
        "x1": 465.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "EVIDENCE, SAYS PRIME MINISTER"
      },
      {
        "y": 529.5,
        "x0": 89.2,
        "x1": 302.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "SUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT3 THE ONLY ANSWER FOR"
      },
      {
        "y": 542.6,
        "x0": 106.9,
        "x1": 285.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "EMERGING COUNTRIES, SAYS UN COMMISSION"
      },
      {
        "y": 561.3,
        "x0": 334.2,
        "x1": 509.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "RENEWABLE ENERGY4 – GOVERNMENT DEVELOPS"
      },
      {
        "y": 573.1,
        "x0": 394.9,
        "x1": 448.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "NEW STRATEGY"
      },
      {
        "y": 598.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 444.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 reputation for positive support of the environment and for making policies that reflect this"
      },
      {
        "y": 610.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 440.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 people who always make the most depressing or pessimistic predictions about the future"
      },
      {
        "y": 622.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 development of industry, etc. which does not damage the environment or social and economic stability, and"
      },
      {
        "y": 635.7,
        "x0": 104.3,
        "x1": 258.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "which can continue over a period of time"
      },
      {
        "y": 646.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 515.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 energy produced using sun, wind or crops rather than coal or other fuels which cannot be replaced once used"
      },
      {
        "y": 667.8,
        "x0": 110.7,
        "x1": 219.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Common mistakes"
      },
      {
        "y": 692.2,
        "x0": 111.7,
        "x1": 343.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "People cause damage to the environment (NOT damages)."
      }
